=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The network is fully operational. Bidirectional connectivity between pc1 (195.11.14.2) and pc2 (200.1.1.2) is confirmed with zero packet loss in both directions. The BGP session between router1 (AS 1) and router2 (AS 2) is stable and has correctly exchanged routes: router1 holds a BGP route for 200.1.1.0/24 via 193.10.11.2, and router2 holds a BGP route for 195.11.14.0/24 via 193.10.11.1. Both host default gateways are correctly pointed at their respective router interfaces. IP forwarding is enabled on both routers, no iptables rules block forwarding or apply NAT on the data path, and rp_filter is disabled. A BGP OPEN processing error appears in router2's startup log, but this is attributable to a TCP connection collision (both routers initiated simultaneously), resolved automatically by BGP collision detection — the surviving session exchanged all routes correctly. Both routers re-advertise eBGP-learned routes back to their sole eBGP peer, which is standard BGP propagation behavior; AS-PATH loop prevention correctly rejects these reflected routes on receipt ("DENIED due to: as-path contains our own AS"). No blackhole routes, static misconfigurations, wrong prefixes, or policy filters exist. The user's reported symptom of one-way connectivity cannot be reproduced in the current lab state and was most likely a transient perception during the brief BGP session initialization window.
=== END ===